Here's an example of how you could create a browserified bundle of a React application using the `react-randomized` library:
```
// Import the necessary libraries
import React from 'react';
import { render } from 'react-dom';
import Randomized from 'react-randomized';

// Define the component that will be rendered
class App extends React.Component {
  constructor(props) {
    super(props);
    this.state = {
      text: '',
      image: ''
    };
  }

  // Function to generate randomized content
  generateRandomContent() {
    const text = Randomized.text();
    const image = Randomized.image();
    this.setState({ text, image });
  }

