```
import { StyleSheet } from 'react-native';
import csstoxjs from 'csstoxjs';

const convertCSStoStyles = (cssText) => {
  const styles = csstoxjs(cssText);
  return StyleSheet.create(styles);
};
```
This code defines a function `convertCSStoStyles` that takes a CSS text string as input and returns a React Native stylesheet object using the `csstoxjs` library to parse the CSS and create the necessary style objects. The `StyleSheet.create()` method is used to create a new stylesheet from the parsed CSS.

Note: This code assumes that you have already installed the `csstoxjs` library in your project. If you haven't, you can install it using npm by running the command `npm install csstoxjs`.

```
const cssToJs = require('csstoxjs');

function convertCssToReactNativeStyles(cssText) {
  const styles = {};
  const parsedCss = cssToJs(cssText);

  for (const rule of parsedCss.rules) {
    const styleName = rule.selectorText;
    const styleValue = rule.style;

    if (!styles[styleName]) {
      styles[styleName] = {};
    }

    for (const property in styleValue) {
      const value = styleValue[property];

      switch (property) {
        case 'color':
          styles[styleName].color = value;
          break;
        case 'fontSize':
          styles[styleName].fontSize = value;
          break;
        case 'fontWeight':
          styles[styleName].fontWeight = value;
          break;
        default:
          console.warn(`Unsupported property ${property} in CSS rule ${rule}`);
      }
    }
  }

  return styles;
}
```
This code uses the `csstoxjs` library to parse the input CSS text and create a React Native stylesheet object. It loops through each CSS rule and creates a new style object for each selector, with properties set based on the CSS property names and values. If a property is not supported by React Native, it logs a warning message.

Here's an example of how you can use the `dns-sd` module to encode and decode DNS-SD TXT record RDATA fields in Node.js:
```javascript
const dns = require('dns-sd');

// Encode a TXT record RDATA field
const encodedTxtRecord = dns.encodeTxtRecord({
  'key1': 'value1',
  'key2': 'value2'
});
console.log(encodedTxtRecord); // Output: "key1=value1,key2=value2"

// Decode a TXT record RDATA field
