const addSourceProp = (node) => {
  if (node.type === 'JSXElement') {
    node.props.__source = true;
  } else if (node.children) {
    for (let child of node.children) {
      addSourceProp(child);
    }
  }
};
```
This code defines a mutator function `addSourceProp` that takes a JSX element as an argument and adds the `__source` prop to it if it is not already present. The function recursively traverses all child nodes of the given node and updates their props with the `__source` prop.

To use this code, you can call the `addSourceProp` function on a JSX element like this:
```
const element = <div>Hello World</div>;
addSourceProp(element);
console.log(element); // Output: <div __source={true}>Hello World</div>
```
Alternatively, you can use a library like `jsx-transformer` to modify the JSX syntax and add the `__source` prop to all elements in your codebase. This can be done by installing the library using npm or yarn and then running it on your codebase with the appropriate options.
