The `runTask` function takes two arguments: the name of the task to be run, and any number of additional arguments that will be passed to the task function when it is invoked. It first checks if a task with the given name exists in the `tasks` object, and throws an error if it does not. If the task exists, it invokes the task function with the given arguments and returns its result.

