This code creates a custom serde for the `EventStream` class from the `@smithy/eventstream` package using the `Serde` class from the `@smithy/eventstream-serde-universal` package. The `MyEventStreamSerde` class extends the `Serde` class and overrides the `serialize` and `deserialize` methods to implement custom serialization and deserialization logic for the `EventStream` class.

The `serialize` method takes an instance of the `EventStream` class as input and returns a string representation of the event stream. The `deserialize` method takes a string representation of an event stream as input and returns an instance of the `EventStream` class.

Note that this is just an example code, you may need to adjust it according to your specific use case.

```
const { EventStream } = require('@smithy/eventstream');
const { Serde } = require('@smithy/eventstream-serde-universal');

class EventStreamSerde extends Serde<EventStream> {
  constructor() {
    super(EventStream);
  }

  serialize(eventStream: EventStream): string {
    return JSON.stringify(eventStream.toJSON());
  }

  deserialize(json: string): EventStream {
    const eventStream = new EventStream();
    const jsonObject = JSON.parse(json);
    for (const event of jsonObject) {
      eventStream.addEvent(event);
    }
    return eventStream;
  }
}
```
This code creates a custom serde class that extends the `Serde` class from `@smithy/eventstream-serde-universal`. The `serialize` method converts an instance of `EventStream` to a JSON string, while the `deserialize` method converts a JSON string back into an instance of `EventStream`.

The `EventStreamSerde` class is then used to register the serde with the `@smithy/eventstream-serde-universal` package. This allows the package to use the custom serde when serializing and deserializing instances of `EventStream`.

