function generateJavaScriptCode(ast) {
  const code = parse(ast);
  return code;
}

module.exports = { generateJavaScriptCode };
```
This code uses the `parse` function from the `escodegen` library to convert the AST into equivalent JavaScript code, and then returns the generated code. The `traverse` function from the `estree-util` library is used to traverse the AST and transform it into the desired format.

Note that this code assumes that the input AST is in a valid format and can be parsed by the `escodegen` library. If the AST contains errors or is not in a valid format, the generated JavaScript code may also contain errors or behave unexpectedly.

```
const escodegen = require('escodegen');
const estreeUtil = require('estree-util');

function generateJavaScriptCode(ast) {
  const code = estreeUtil.traverse(ast, {
    enter(node) {
      // Handle each node type and generate the corresponding JavaScript code
      switch (node.type) {
        case 'Program':
          return `const ${node.body[0].name} = ${generateJavaScriptCode(node.body[0])};`;
        case 'VariableDeclaration':
          return `${node.declarations[0].id.name} = ${generateJavaScriptCode(node.declarations[0].init)};`;
        case 'FunctionDeclaration':
          return `function ${node.id.name}(${node.params.map((param) => param.name).join(', ')}) {${generateJavaScriptCode(node.body)}}`;
        default:
          throw new Error(`Unsupported node type: ${node.type}`);
      }
    },
  });

  return code;
}
```
This code uses the `escodegen` and `estree-util` libraries to traverse the AST and generate equivalent JavaScript code for each node in the tree. The `generateJavaScriptCode` function takes an AST as input and returns a string of JavaScript code that represents the same program.

The `enter` method is called for each node in the AST, and it generates the corresponding JavaScript code based on the node type. For example, if the node is a `Program`, it will generate a variable declaration with an initializer. If the node is a `FunctionDeclaration`, it will generate a function definition with parameters and a body.

The `generateJavaScriptCode` function uses the `estree-util` library to traverse the AST and generate the corresponding JavaScript code for each node. The `escodegen` library is used to generate the final JavaScript code from the generated code.

Note that this code only handles a limited set of node types, and it may not work correctly for all possible input ASTs. It is also important to note that this code does not handle any errors or edge cases, and it should be tested thoroughly before being used in production.

