const mda = require('mda');

function findAndReplace(tree, searchValue, replaceValue) {
  const result = [];
  mda.traverse(tree, (node) => {
    if (node.type === 'text' && node.value === searchValue) {
      result.push(node);
    }
  });
  return result;
}
```
This code uses the `mda` library to traverse through a tree data structure and find all nodes with the specified text value. The `findAndReplace` function takes three arguments: `tree`, which is the root node of the tree, `searchValue`, which is the text value to search for, and `replaceValue`, which is the new text value to replace the matched values with.

The function uses the `traverse` method provided by the `mda` library to recursively traverse through the branches and leaves of the tree, and checks each node's type and value against the specified search value. If a match is found, the function pushes the node into an array that will be returned at the end of the traversal.

Once the traversal is complete, the `findAndReplace` function returns the array of matched nodes, which can then be used to update the text values in the tree.

