const esbuild = require('esbuild');

module.exports = {
  plugins: [
    {
      name: 'path-aliases',
      setup(build) {
        build.onResolve({ filter: /^@\// }, (args) => {
          const alias = args.path.replace(/^@\//, '');
          return { path: `${process.cwd()}/${alias}`, namespace: 'path-aliases' };
        });
      }
    }
  ]
};
```
This code defines a plugin for Esbuild that allows for the use of path aliases in the build process. The plugin uses the `onResolve` hook to intercept all imports that start with `@/` and replace them with the actual file path relative to the project root. For example, if an import is made from a file at `/src/index.js` using the alias `@/components/Button`, the plugin will resolve it to `/src/components/Button`.

The plugin also sets the `namespace` property of the resolved path to `'path-aliases'`, which allows Esbuild to differentiate between this type of import and other types of imports.

To use this plugin, you can add it to your Esbuild configuration like so:
