const { Pool } = require('node-pool');

// Create a new resource pool with a maximum size of 10
const pool = new Pool(10);

// Acquire a resource from the pool
async function acquireResource() {
  const resource = await pool.acquire();
  return resource;
}

// Release a resource back to the pool
async function releaseResource(resource) {
  pool.release(resource);
}
```
This code creates a new resource pool with a maximum size of 10 using the `node-pool` package. The `acquire()` method is used to acquire a resource from the pool, and the `release()` method is used to release a resource back to the pool. These methods are asynchronous, so they can be used in an async function.

This code allows multiple clients to safely acquire and release resources without overloading the server. The resource pool ensures that there is always a certain number of available resources, even if multiple clients try to access them at the same time.

