// Instrument HTTP and HTTPS requests using OpenTelemetry API
const { HttpInstrumentation } = require('opentelemetry-instrumentation');
const instrumentation = new HttpInstrumentation();

// Set up a tracer provider
const { TracerProvider } = require('@opentelemetry/api');
const tracerProvider = new TracerProvider();

// Create a tracer
const tracer = tracerProvider.getTracer('my-tracer', '1.0');

// Set up the instrumentation to use the tracer
instrumentation.setTracer(tracer);

// Start the instrumentation
instrumentation.start();
```
This code sets up an instance of the `HttpInstrumentation` class from the OpenTelemetry API, which is used to instrument HTTP and HTTPS requests. It then creates a tracer provider and a tracer using the `@opentelemetry/api` package, and sets the tracer on the instrumentation instance. Finally, it starts the instrumentation by calling the `start()` method.

This code will automatically instrument all HTTP and HTTPS requests made by your web application, providing detailed performance metrics and distributed tracing for your application.

