Here is an example of how you could create a set of reusable React components for interacting with maps rendered using Mapbox GL JS:
```
import React from 'react';
import { MapboxGL } from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-js';

// Create a component that renders a map and allows the user to add markers, popups, and overlays.
class Map extends React.Component {
  constructor(props) {
    super(props);
    this.state = {
      // Initialize the map with some default settings.
      map: new MapboxGL({
        container: 'map',
        style: 'https://api.mapbox.com/styles/v1/mapbox/streets-v11?optimize=true&access_token=YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN',
        center: [-74.50, 40],
        zoom: 13
      })
    };
  }

  // Add a marker to the map at a specific location.
  addMarker(latitude, longitude) {
    const marker = new MapboxGL.Marker({
      position: [longitude, latitude]
    });
    this.state.map.addLayer(marker);
  }

  // Add a popup to the map at a specific location with some text.
  addPopup(latitude, longitude, text) {
    const popup = new MapboxGL.Popup({
      position: [longitude, latitude],
      offset: 25,
      closeButton: true,
      closeOnClick: false
    });
    popup.setHTML(text);
    this.state.map.addLayer(popup);
  }

  // Add an overlay to the map with some text and a click handler.
  addOverlay(latitude, longitude, text, onClick) {
    const overlay = new MapboxGL.Popup({
      position: [longitude, latitude],
      offset: 25,
      closeButton: true,
      closeOnClick: false
    });
    overlay.setHTML(text);
    overlay.on('click', onClick);
    this.state.map.addLayer(overlay);
  }

  render() {
    return (
      <div>
        <div id="map" style={{ width: '100%', height: '400px' }} />
        <button onClick={() => this.addMarker(-74.50, 40)}>Add Marker</button>
        <button onClick={() => this.addPopup(-74.50, 40, 'Hello World!')}>Add Popup</button>
        <button onClick={() => this.addOverlay(-74.50, 40, 'Click Me!', () => console.log('You clicked the overlay.'))}>Add Overlay</button>
      </div>
    );
  }
}
```
This component uses the `MapboxGL` library to create a map and add markers, popups, and overlays. The `addMarker`, `addPopup`, and `addOverlay` methods are used to add these elements to the map. The `render` method returns a React element that includes a div with an ID of "map" where the map will be rendered, as well as buttons for adding markers, popups, and overlays.

You can use this component in your app by importing it and rendering it in your JSX code:
```
import React from 'react';
import { Map } from './Map';

function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Map />
    </div>
  );
}
```
This will render the map and allow you to add markers, popups, and overlays using the buttons in the component.

