To create an interactive in-browser GraphQL IDE using React, Redux, and GraphQL, you can follow these steps:

1. Set up a GraphQL server: You will need to set up a GraphQL server that exposes your GraphQL schema and allows clients to send queries and mutations. There are many libraries available for this purpose, such as Apollo Server or Prisma.
2. Create a React app: You can use create-react-app to create a new React app and install the necessary dependencies, including Redux.
3. Set up Redux: You will need to set up Redux in your React app to manage the state of your GraphQL queries and mutations. You can use the Redux library to create a store that holds the state of your GraphQL queries and mutations.
4. Create a GraphQL client: You will need to create a GraphQL client that sends queries and mutations to your GraphQL server. You can use a library like apollo-client to create a GraphQL client that communicates with your GraphQL server.
5. Implement syntax highlighting, code completion, and real-time query results display: To implement these features, you will need to use libraries like CodeMirror or Ace Editor to provide syntax highlighting and code completion for your GraphQL queries and mutations. You can also use a library like React Query to display the results of your GraphQL queries in real-time.
6. Test and deploy: Once you have implemented the features, you will need to test them thoroughly to ensure that they work as expected. After testing, you can deploy your app to a production environment.

