    if (decl.value.includes('w3c-color')) {
      decl.value = decl.value.replace(/w3c-color\(\s*['"]?([a-z]+)['"]?\s*\)/g, '$1');
    }
  });
  return root.toString();
}

module.exports = postcss.plugin('w3c-color-functions', () => {
  return (root) => {
    root.walkDecls((decl) => {
      decl.value = w3cColorFunctionsToCompatibleCSS(decl.value);
    });
  };
});
```
This code uses the PostCSS API to create a plugin that transforms W3C CSS color functions into more compatible CSS, allowing for smoother integration with modern web technologies. The `w3cColorFunctionsToCompatibleCSS` function takes in a string of CSS and returns a new string with the W3C color functions replaced by their compatible counterparts.

The plugin itself is created using the `postcss.plugin` method, which takes two arguments: the name of the plugin (in this case, `'w3c-color-functions'`) and a function that will be called for each declaration in the CSS file. In this case, the function simply calls the `w3cColorFunctionsToCompatibleCSS` function on each declaration value and returns the result.

This plugin can then be used with PostCSS to transform W3C color functions in your CSS files into more compatible syntax. For example:
```
