```
Once installed, you can add the following configuration to your Webpack config file:
```
const HtmlIncludeAssetsPlugin = require('html-include-assets-plugin');

module.exports = {
  // ... other config options ...
  plugins: [
    new HtmlIncludeAssetsPlugin({
      assets: ['partials/**/*.html'],
      append: true,
    }),
  ],
};
```
This will include all HTML files in the `partials` directory and its subdirectories into your main HTML file. The `append` option tells Webpack to append the included assets to the end of the main HTML file.

You can then use the `html-webpack-plugin` to compile your HTML files, which will include the partials as well. For example:
```
const HtmlWebpackPlugin = require('html-webpack-plugin');

