    expect(widget.render).toHaveBeenCalledWith("dataForWidget");
    expect(otherStuff).toHaveHappened();
  });
});
```
In this example, we create a mock implementation of the `getDataFromServer` function using the `Promise.resolve()` method to return a resolved promise with the value `'mockData'`. We then replace the imported function with the mock implementation using the `__set__()` method provided by Mocha + Babel.

This allows us to test the `Widget` class without actually making any HTTP requests or relying on the real implementation of the `getDataFromServer` function.

