```
This will start the task and reload the data for the record with ID 2 from the server.

To reload an Ember Data record from the server, you can use the `reload` method provided by Ember Data. Here's an example of how to do it:
```
// Assuming you have a model called "MyRecord" and a route called "my-record"
import Route from '@ember/routing/route';
import { inject as service } from '@ember/service';

export default class MyRecordRoute extends Route {
