response_prompt:
To set up Google Analytics through Google Tag Manager for Next.js, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new container in your Google Tag Manager account and select "Web" as the platform.
2. In the container settings, add a new tag with the type "Google Analytics".
3. In the tag settings, enter your Google Analytics tracking ID (UA-*******-*) and set the "Page View" trigger to "All Pages".
4. Save and publish the container.
5. In your Next.js app, add the following code to your header component:
```
import { useEffect } from 'react';
import { gtag } from '@google-analytics/gtag';

const initGA = () => {
  gtag('config', 'UA-*******-*');
};

const logPageView = () => {
  gtag('event', 'page_view', { page: window.location.pathname });
};

export const Header = () => {
  useEffect(() => {
    if (!window.GA_INITIALIZED) {
      initGA();
      window.GA_INITIALIZED = true;
    }
    logPageView();
  }, []);

  return (
    <div>
      <h1>My App</h1>
    </div>
  );
};
```
In this code, we're using the `@google-analytics/gtag` package to initialize and log page views in Google Analytics. We're also using the `useEffect` hook to ensure that the GA initialization and page view logging are only executed once per session.

