  for (let y = 0; y < height; y++) {
    for (let x = 0; x < width; x++) {
      const Y = pFrame.data[0][x + y * width];
      const Cr = pFrame.data[1][x / 2 + ((int)(y / 2)) * pFrame.linesize[1]];
      const Cb = pFrame.data[2][x / 2 + ((int)(y / 2)) * pFrame.linesize[2]];
      const [R, G, B] = YCrCb_to_RGB8(Y, Cr, Cb);
      wrap.writeUInt8(R, x * 3 + 0);
      wrap.writeUInt8(G, x * 3 + 1);
      wrap.writeUInt8(B, x * 3 + 2);
    }
  }
}

function save_RGB_frame(buffer, filename) {
  const image = new Image();
  image.width = buffer.width;
  image.height = buffer.height;
  image.data = buffer.data;
  imageSave(image, 'ppm', filename);
}
```
I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any questions or need further assistance.

You can use the following JavaScript packages to play a video with captions in Jupyter notebook:

* `video.js`: A JavaScript library for playing videos in web browsers. It supports various video formats and provides an API for adding captions.
* `subtitle.js`: A JavaScript library for displaying subtitles on top of videos. It can be used to display captions for videos played using the `video.js` library.
* `jupyter-videoplayer`: A Jupyter notebook extension that provides a video player widget for playing videos in Jupyter notebooks. It supports various video formats and provides an API for adding captions.

You can install these packages using npm or yarn, depending on your preference:
```
npm install video.js subtitle.js jupyter-videoplayer
```
or
```
yarn add video.js subtitle.js jupyter-videoplayer
```
Once you have installed the packages, you can use them in your Jupyter notebook to play videos with captions. Here is an example of how to use `video.js` and `subtitle.js` to display a video with captions:
```
import { Video } from 'video.js';
import { Subtitles } from 'subtitle.js';

// Create a new Video object
const video = new Video('my-video');

// Load the video file and add it to the player
video.load('team-rocket.video-compressed.mp4');

// Add subtitles to the video
const subtitle = new Subtitles();
subtitle.add({
  language: 'en',
  text: 'This is a test caption'
});
video.addSubtitle(subtitle);

// Play the video
video.play();
```
You can also use `jupyter-videoplayer` to play videos with captions in Jupyter notebook. Here is an example of how to use it:
```
import { VideoPlayer } from 'jupyter-videoplayer';

// Create a new VideoPlayer object
const player = new VideoPlayer('my-video');

// Load the video file and add it to the player
player.load('team-rocket.video-compressed.mp4');

// Add subtitles to the video
player.addSubtitle({
  language: 'en',
  text: 'This is a test caption'
});

// Play the video
player.play();
```

