response_prompt:
The issue is that you are defining the `AngleIcon` component inside the `SectionTab` component, which means that a new instance of the `AngleIcon` component will be created every time the `SectionTab` component renders. This can cause performance issues and may also lead to unexpected behavior in your application.

To fix this issue, you should move the definition of the `AngleIcon` component outside of the `SectionTab` component. Here's an example of how you could do this:
```
import Select from "@mui/material/Select";
import { FontAwesomeIcon } from "@fortawesome/react-fontawesome";
import { faAngleDown } from "@fortawesome/pro-solid-svg-icons/faAngleDown";

const AngleIcon = ({ props }: { props: any }) => {
  return (
    <FontAwesomeIcon icon={faAngleDown} />
  );
};

const SectionTab = () => {
  return (
    <Select
      variant="standard"
      defaultValue="cr"
      disableUnderline
      IconComponent={AngleIcon}
    />
  );
};

export default SectionTab;
```
In this example, the `AngleIcon` component is defined outside of the `SectionTab` component, so it will only be created once when the application starts. Then, you can pass a reference to the `AngleIcon` component as the `IconComponent` prop of the `Select` component inside the `SectionTab` component. This way, you can avoid creating a new instance of the `AngleIcon` component every time the `SectionTab` component renders.

