I would like to know how I can convert the Mongo document into a downloadable file. Thanks

response_prompt:
You can use the `mongodb` package to interact with MongoDB from your Node.js application. Here's an example of how you could use it to download a file stored in MongoDB:
```
const mongodb = require('mongodb');

// Connect to the MongoDB server
const client = new mongodb.MongoClient(url, { useNewUrlParser: true });
client.connect((err) => {
  if (err) throw err;

  // Get the file from the database
  const db = client.db(databaseName);
  const collection = db.collection('files');
  const fileId = 'your_file_id';
  collection.findOne({ _id: fileId }, (err, doc) => {
    if (err) throw err;

    // Convert the binary data to a Buffer
    const buffer = new Uint8Array(doc.data);

    // Create a readable stream from the buffer
    const stream = new mongodb.ReadableStream({ objectMode: true });
    stream.push(buffer);
    stream.push(null);

    // Pipe the stream to a file on disk
    const outputFile = fs.createWriteStream('path/to/output/file');
    stream.pipe(outputFile);
  });
});
```
This code connects to the MongoDB server, finds the file in the `files` collection with the specified `_id`, converts the binary data to a Buffer, creates a readable stream from the buffer, and pipes the stream to a file on disk using the `fs.createWriteStream()` method.

You can also use the `mongodb-streams` package to handle the streaming of data between MongoDB and your application. Here's an example of how you could use it to download a file stored in MongoDB:
```
const mongodb = require('mongodb');
const mongodbStreams = require('mongodb-streams');

// Connect to the MongoDB server
const client = new mongodb.MongoClient(url, { useNewUrlParser: true });
client.connect((err) => {
  if (err) throw err;

  // Get the file from the database
  const db = client.db(databaseName);
  const collection = db.collection('files');
  const fileId = 'your_file_id';
  collection.findOne({ _id: fileId }, (err, doc) => {
    if (err) throw err;

    // Create a readable stream from the MongoDB cursor
    const stream = mongodbStreams.createReadableStream(collection, { objectMode: true });

    // Pipe the stream to a file on disk
    const outputFile = fs.createWriteStream('path/to/output/file');
    stream.pipe(outputFile);
  });
});
```
This code is similar to the previous example, but it uses the `mongodb-streams` package to create a readable stream from the MongoDB cursor, which allows you to handle the streaming of data between MongoDB and your application more efficiently.

