How can I obtain the second design in which each field is separated?

response_prompt:
You can use the following JavaScript packages to achieve the desired styling for your Stripe credit card fields:

* "stripe-elements": This package provides a way to customize the appearance of Stripe elements, including credit card fields. You can use it to create a custom style for your credit card fields and separate each field into its own container.
* "stripe-js": This package is used to interact with the Stripe API and handle payments. It provides a way to create a Stripe element, which you can then customize using the "stripe-elements" package.
* "bootstrap": This package provides a way to style your HTML elements using Bootstrap classes. You can use it to create a responsive design for your credit card fields and separate each field into its own container.

Here is an example of how you could use these packages to achieve the desired styling:
```
// Import the necessary packages
import { Stripe, Elements } from "stripe-js";
import { createElement } from "stripe-elements";
import { Card } from "bootstrap";

// Initialize Stripe and create an elements instance
const stripe = Stripe("YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY");
const elements = stripe.elements();

// Create a custom style for your credit card fields
const style = {
  base: {
    color: "#32325d",
    fontFamily: '"Helvetica Neue", Helvetica, sans-serif',
    fontSmoothing: "antialiased",
    fontSize: "16px",
    "::placeholder": {
      color: "#aab7c4"
    }
  },
  invalid: {
    color: "#fa755a",
    iconColor: "#fa755a"
  }
};

// Create a Stripe element and mount it to the DOM
const card = elements.create("card", { hidePostalCode: true, style });
card.mount("#card-element");

// Use Bootstrap to create a responsive design for your credit card fields
const cardContainer = document.getElementById("card-container");
const cardElement = document.createElement("div");
cardElement.classList.add("card", "mb-3");
cardContainer.appendChild(cardElement);

// Create separate containers for each field in the credit card form
const nameInput = document.createElement("input");
nameInput.type = "text";
nameInput.placeholder = "Name on Card";
nameInput.classList.add("form-control", "mb-3");
cardElement.appendChild(nameInput);

const numberInput = document.createElement("input");
numberInput.type = "text";
numberInput.placeholder = "Card Number";
numberInput.classList.add("form-control", "mb-3");
cardElement.appendChild(numberInput);

const expiryInput = document.createElement("input");
expiryInput.type = "text";
expiryInput.placeholder = "Expiration Date";
expiryInput.classList.add("form-control", "mb-3");
cardElement.appendChild(expiryInput);

const cvcInput = document.createElement("input");
cvcInput.type = "text";
cvcInput.placeholder = "CVC";
cvcInput.classList.add("form-control", "mb-3");
cardElement.appendChild(cvcInput);
```
This code creates a custom style for your credit card fields using the "stripe-elements" package, and then uses Bootstrap to create a responsive design for your credit card form. It also separates each field into its own container using JavaScript.

