Here are some JavaScript packages that you can use to set up a WebSocket server in SvelteKit using the `ws` package:

* `ws`: A simple, lightweight WebSocket library for Node.js and browsers.
* `svelte-websocket`: A Svelte component for connecting to WebSockets.
* `svelte-websockets`: A Svelte plugin for handling WebSocket connections.

Here's an example of how you can use the `ws` package to set up a WebSocket server in SvelteKit:
```
import { Server } from 'ws';

const webSocketServer = new Server({ port: 8080 });

webSocketServer.on('connection', (socket) => {
  console.log(`Client connected: ${socket.remoteAddress}:${socket.remotePort}`);
});
```
This will create a WebSocket server that listens on port 8080 and logs when a client connects. You can then use the `ws` package to handle incoming messages from clients and send responses back to them.

Here's an example of how you can use the `svelte-websocket` component to set up a WebSocket connection in SvelteKit:
```
import { WebSocket } from 'svelte-websocket';

const webSocket = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:8080');

webSocket.onmessage = (event) => {
  console.log(`Received message: ${event.data}`);
};
```
This will create a WebSocket connection to the server running on `http://localhost:8080` and log any incoming messages from the server. You can then use the `ws` package to handle incoming messages from clients and send responses back to them.

Here's an example of how you can use the `svelte-websockets` plugin to set up a WebSocket connection in SvelteKit:
```
import { websockets } from 'svelte-websockets';

const webSocket = new websockets.WebSocket('ws://localhost:8080');

webSocket.onmessage = (event) => {
  console.log(`Received message: ${event.data}`);
};
```
This will create a WebSocket connection to the server running on `http://localhost:8080` and log any incoming messages from the server. You can then use the `ws` package to handle incoming messages from clients and send responses back to them.

I hope this helps! Let me know if you have any questions or need further assistance.

