To get the `FormData` from the payload in your server-side component, you can use the `readMultipartFormData()` method provided by Nuxt.js. This method allows you to read the form data from the request body and return it as a `FormData` object.

Here's an example of how you can modify your code to get the `FormData` from the payload:
```javascript
import { InnoDB } from 'inno-db';
import { defineEventHandler, readMultipartFormData } from '@nuxt/server';

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const payload = await readMultipartFormData(event);
  const formData = payload.formData;

  // Get the file contents as a Buffer object
  const fileContents = formData.get('userFile').buffer();

  // Create a new InnoDB instance with the file contents
  const dbFileInstance = new InnoDb({
    id: InnoDB.autoGenerate,
    File: fileContents,
    FileName: formData.get('fileName'),
    Content-Type: formData.get('fileType'),
    TTL: formData.get('fileTTL')
  });

  // Save the file to the database
  dbFileInstance.save((doc, err) => {
    if (err) {
      console.log(err);
    } else {
      console.log(`File saved successfully: ${doc._id}`);
    }
  });
});
```
In this example, we first read the form data from the request body using `readMultipartFormData()`. We then get the file contents as a Buffer object by calling the `buffer()` method on the `userFile` field of the `formData` object.

We then create a new InnoDB instance with the file contents and save it to the database using the `save()` method. If there is an error saving the file, we log it to the console. Otherwise, we log a success message indicating that the file was saved successfully.

