Here is an example of how you can use this package in your client-side code:
```
import { Logger } from 'gcp-logging';

const logger = new Logger('my-app');
logger.log('Hello, world!');
```
This will log the message "Hello, world!" to Google Cloud Logging with the name of the logger set to "my-app". You can also use other methods such as `info()`, `warn()`, and `error()` to log different types of messages.

Note that this package requires a valid GCP project ID and service account credentials to be set up in your browser's environment variables or configuration files. You can find more information on how to set these up in the `gcp-logging` documentation.

