response_prompt:
Here are some JavaScript packages that could be helpful in implementing a mouse wheel zoom-in/zoom-out function for Highcharts in React:

* `highcharts-react-official` - This package provides a wrapper component for using Highcharts with React. It includes support for mouse wheel zooming out of the box.
* `highcharts-react-wrapper` - This package provides a more flexible way to use Highcharts with React by allowing you to pass in your own options and callbacks. It also includes support for mouse wheel zooming.
* `react-highcharts` - This package provides a simple way to use Highcharts with React by allowing you to pass in your own data and options. It also includes support for mouse wheel zooming.

You can install these packages using npm or yarn:
```
npm install highcharts-react-official
npm install highcharts-react-wrapper
npm install react-highcharts
```
Once you have installed the package, you can use it in your React component like this:
```
import HighCharts from 'highcharts-react-official';

const options = {
  title: {
    text: 'Monthly Average Temperature',
    x: -20, // center
  },
  subtitle: {
    text: 'Source: WorldClimate.com',
    x: -20,
  },
  xAxis: {
    /*
    categories: ['Jan']
    */
  },
  yAxis: {
    title: {
      text: 'Temperature (¡ÆC)',
    },
    plotLines: [{
      value: 0,
      width: 1,
      color: '#808080',
    }],
  },
  tooltip: {
    valueSuffix: '¡ÆC',
  },
  legend: {
    layout: 'vertical',
    align: 'right',
    verticalAlign: 'middle',
    borderWidth: 0,
  },
  series: [{
    name: 'Tokyo',
    data: [],
  }, {
    name: 'New York',
    data: [],
  }, {
    name: 'Berlin',
    data: [],
  }, {
    name: 'London',
    data: [],
  }],
  zoomType: 'x',
};

const HighChartTest = () => {
  const chartComponentRef = useRef(null);
  const [options, setoptions] = useState(option);
  let now = new Date(1997, 9, 3);
  let value = Math.random() * 1000;
  const oneDay = 24 * 3600 * 1000;

  const chartData: any = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
  const chartData1: any = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
  const chartData2: any = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
  const chartData3: any = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
  for (let i = 0; i {
    chartComponentRef.current?.chart.series[0].setData(chartData);
    chartComponentRef.current?.chart.series[1].setData(chartData1);
    chartComponentRef.current?.chart.series[2].setData(chartData2);
    chartComponentRef.current?.chart.series[3].setData(chartData3);
  }, []);

  return (
    <HighCharts options={options} ref={chartComponentRef} />
  );
};
```
In this example, we are using the `highcharts-react-official` package to render a Highcharts chart in our React component. We are also using the `useState` hook to store the chart options and the `useRef` hook to reference the chart instance.

To enable mouse wheel zooming, you can add the following code to your chart options:
```
zoomType: 'x',
scrollbar: {
  enabled: true,
},
```
This will allow users to use the mouse wheel to zoom in and out of the chart. You can also customize the scrollbar appearance by adding additional options, such as `scrollbar.height` or `scrollbar.background`.

Note that you may need to adjust the `zoomType` option depending on your specific use case. For example, if you want to allow users to zoom in and out of the chart using the mouse wheel while also allowing them to pan the chart, you can set `zoomType` to `'xy'`.

