The issue is likely due to the fact that the `availableAppDefinitions` getter is not marked as a dependent key of the `selectedAppCategories` property. This means that Ember does not know that the getter depends on the value of `selectedAppCategories`, and therefore it will not be recomputed when the value of `selectedAppCategories` changes.

To fix this, you can add the `selectedAppCategories` property as a dependent key to the `availableAppDefinitions` getter using the `@dependentKeyCompatible` decorator. This will tell Ember that the getter depends on the value of `selectedAppCategories`, and it will be recomputed when the value of `selectedAppCategories` changes.

Here is an example of how you can modify your code to use the `@dependentKeyCompatible` decorator:
```
import { inject as service } from '@ember/service';
import { action } from '@ember/object';
import { tracked } from '@glimmer/tracking';
import Controller from '@ember/controller';
import { A } from '@ember/array';

export default class IntegrationActivationIndexController extends Controller {
