To make ember-bootstrap and ember-power-select work together, you need to add a few dependencies to your project. Here are the steps:

1. Install ember-popperjs: This is a dependency that provides the popover functionality for ember-bootstrap. You can install it by running the following command in your terminal:
```bash
ember install ember-popperjs
```
2. Add the popperjs library to your project's `ember-cli-build.js` file:
```javascript
module.exports = function(defaults, env) {
  let app = new EmberApp(defaults, {
    // Add the popperjs library to the list of dependencies
    'popperjs': true
  });

  return app.toTree();
};
```
3. In your template, use the `BsPopover` component and pass in the `target` property as a reference to the element that you want to display the popover near:
```handlebars
<div>
  {{#bs-popover target="myTargetElement"}}
    <p>This is the content of the popover</p>
  {{/bs-popover}}
</div>
```
4. In your JavaScript file, define a reference to the element that you want to display the popover near:
```javascript
import Component from '@ember/component';
import { action } from '@ember/object';

export default class MyComponent extends Component {
  // Define a reference to the target element
  myTargetElement = null;

  @action
  setup() {
    this.myTargetElement = document.getElementById('target-element');
  }
}
```
5. In your CSS file, add the following styles to make sure that the popover is displayed correctly:
```css
/* Add these styles to make sure that the popover is displayed correctly */
.popover {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0;
  left: 0;
}

.popover-content {
  padding: 1rem;
}
```
With these steps, you should be able to use ember-bootstrap and ember-power-select together in your project.

