const scope = angularElement.scope();
scope.$ctrl[myFunction]();
```
Note that you will need to have the `playwright-angular` package installed in order to use the `angular` object, which provides a way to interact with Angular applications using Playwright. You can install this package using npm:
```
npm install playwright-angular
