You can use the following JavaScript packages to extract only specific elements and combine `find_all` and `find_elements_by_xpath`:

* `cheerio-selectors`: This package provides a simple and efficient way to select elements based on CSS selectors. You can use it to select elements that match a certain criteria, such as the presence of a specific class or attribute.
* `xpath-selectors`: This package provides a simple and efficient way to select elements based on XPath expressions. You can use it to select elements that match a certain criteria, such as the presence of a specific attribute or text content.

Here is an example of how you could use these packages to extract only specific elements and combine `find_all` and `find_elements_by_xpath`:
```
const cheerio = require('cheerio');
const xpath = require('xpath-selectors');

// Load the HTML page into Cheerio
const $ = cheerio.load(html);

// Select all elements that match a certain CSS selector
const items = $('span[data-test-id^="fdbk-item-"]').toArray();

// Filter the selected elements to only include those with a specific attribute value
const filteredItems = items.filter((item) => {
  return item.attribs['data-test-id'].includes('mirror|tray|ceramic');
});

// Use XPath to select elements within the filtered items
const xpathResults = filteredItems.map((item) => {
  const xpathResult = xpath.select(item, '//div[contains(text(),"mirror|tray|ceramic",flags=re.IGNORECASE)]');
  return xpathResult;
});
```
This code will select all elements that match the CSS selector `span[data-test-id^="fdbk-item-"]`, filter them to only include those with a specific attribute value, and then use XPath to select elements within the filtered items. The resulting XPath results are stored in the `xpathResults` array.

You can use the following JavaScript packages to solve this problem:

* `string-replace`: This package provides a simple and efficient way to replace substrings in strings. You can use it to replace the last four digits of each phone number with their corresponding values plus one.
* `regexp-matcher`: This package allows you to match regular expressions against strings, and extract matches. You can use it to extract the last four digits of each phone number and then replace them with their corresponding values plus one.
* `string-scanner`: This package provides a simple way to scan through a string and extract substrings based on a pattern. You can use it to scan through each line of the input file, extract the last four digits of each phone number, and then replace them with their corresponding values plus one.

Here is an example of how you could use these packages to solve your problem:
```
const stringReplace = require('string-replace');
const regexpMatcher = require('regexp-matcher');
const stringScanner = require('string-scanner');

// Define the regular expression pattern for matching phone numbers
const phoneNumberPattern = /(\+1\d{3}\d{3}\d{4})/g;

// Read the input file and process each line
fs.readFileSync('test.txt', 'utf8').split('\n').forEach(line => {
  // Use string-replace to replace the last four digits of each phone number with their corresponding values plus one
  const replacedLine = stringReplace(line, phoneNumberPattern, (match, p1) => {
    return match.replace(/\d{4}$/, (p1 + 1));
  });

  // Use regexp-matcher to extract the last four digits of each phone number and replace them with their corresponding values plus one
  const matches = regexpMatcher(phoneNumberPattern, line);
  if (matches.length > 0) {
    for (const match of matches) {
      const replacedMatch = match.replace(/\d{4}$/, (match[1] + 1));
      replacedLine = stringReplace(replacedLine, match, replacedMatch);
    }
  }

  // Use string-scanner to scan through each line and extract the last four digits of each phone number
  const scanner = new StringScanner(line);
  while (scanner.scan(/(\+1\d{3}\d{3}\d{4})/)) {
    const replacedMatch = scanner.match[1].replace(/\d{4}$/, (scanner.match[1] + 1));
    replacedLine = stringReplace(replacedLine, scanner.match[0], replacedMatch);
  }

  // Write the replaced line to the output file
  fs.writeFileSync('output.txt', replacedLine + '\n');
});
```
This code will read the input file, process each line, and write the replaced line to the output file. It uses `string-replace` to replace the last four digits of each phone number with their corresponding values plus one, and it also uses `regexp-matcher` to extract the last four digits of each phone number and replace them with their corresponding values plus one. Finally, it uses `string-scanner` to scan through each line and extract the last four digits of each phone number.

