delete require.cache[require.resolve("@x/y")];
this._externalLibrary = require("@x/y");
```
By adding this line to your constructor function, you are deleting the cache for the `externalLibrary` module and then requiring it again, which will cause Node.js to reload the module from disk and create a new instance with its own exports. This should ensure that each instance of `myPanel` has its own independent copy of `externalLibrary`.

