* `phantomjs-cookies`: A package that provides an easy way to enable cookies in PhantomJS.
* `browser-cookies`: A package that provides an easy way to manage cookies in a browser, including support for enabling them.

You can install these packages using npm by running the following commands:
```
npm install puppeteer
npm install playwright
npm install casperjs-cookies
npm install phantomjs-cookies
npm install browser-cookies
```
Once you have installed the package, you can use it in your code to enable cookies for Amazon. For example:
```
const puppeteer = require('puppeteer');

(async () => {
  const browser = await puppeteer.launch();
  const page = await browser.newPage();
  await page.goto('https://www.amazon.com/', { waitUntil: 'networkidle2' });
  await page.setCookie({ name: 'cookie_name', value: 'cookie_value' });
  await browser.close();
})();
```
This code will launch a new instance of Puppeteer, navigate to the Amazon login page, and set a cookie with the specified name and value. You can replace `cookie_name` and `cookie_value` with your own values.

