response_prompt:
To listen for transactions on the Tron blockchain using the WebSocket API, you can use the following code:
```javascript
const TronWeb = require('tron-web');

// Initialize the TronWeb instance with the correct network configuration
const web3 = new TronWeb({
  fullHost: 'https://api.trongrid.io',
  solidityNode: 'https://api.trongrid.io',
  eventServer: 'https://api.trongrid.io/event'
});

// Subscribe to the "transactions" event on the TronWeb instance
web3.eventServer.subscribe('transactions', (error, event) => {
  if (error) {
    console.error('Error subscribing to transaction event:', error);
  } else {
    console.log('New transaction:', event);
  }
});
```
This code will subscribe to the "transactions" event on the TronWeb instance, which will trigger whenever a new transaction is added to the blockchain. The `error` parameter in the callback function will be set to an error object if there was an error subscribing to the event, and the `event` parameter will contain information about the new transaction.

Note that you need to have the correct network configuration for the TronWeb instance to work correctly. You can find more information on how to configure the TronWeb instance in the TronGrid documentation.

